    description: "FILED 2026-09-09 from WI-fasoz (T0a of INV-linub's drain). Record and\ninstrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/t0_sizing_09092026/fasoz/ (PLAN.md\npre-registered, typed_share.py, RESULT.md).\n\nINV-linub recorded swift as \"emit and match in BOTH forms OK\" on WI-nasuf's\n2026-08-05 FIXTURE evidence. Measured on corpus (vapor, a server framework):\n\n    external method-call edges   3,067\n    carrying a receiver TYPE       505   16.5%\n    carrying the `external` sentinel 2,562\n    method-kind rows reached, via swift's OWN edges   11 / 100\n\nTHE MECHANISM WORKS -- so this is a GAP, NOT BLINDNESS, and the distinction is\nthe whole point of filing it separately from scala's cell (0.0%, a refutation).\nTyped module segments are real types: String 36, HTTPHeaders 35,\nEventLoopFuture 23, ChannelHandlerContext 23, ByteBufferAllocator 21,\nHTTPClient 19, FileSystem 15, ByteBuffer 12. Rows genuinely reached include\nChannelHandlerContext.writeAndFlush, FileManager.attributesOfItem and\nEventLoopGroup.syncShutdownGracefully.\n\nWHAT THE UNTYPED 83.5% LOOKS LIKE -- common methods on receivers whose type is\nINFERRED or CHAINED rather than written: get 239, test 167, decode 85,\nwithLockedValue 69, encode 69, map 61, use 51, wait 50, append 48, next 48,\nfirst 48, joined 37.\n\nTHE SHAPE IS PRECEDENTED AND HAS BEEN CLOSED TWICE ELSEWHERE. \"The receiver's\ntype is not written at the call site, and the analyzer tracks it but does not\nroute it into the module slot\" is WI-dizag shape A (rust, closed), INV-mumov /\nWI-zamud (python, worked twice), and WI-garar (objc, filed 2026-09-09 for\n`self.<property>`). Swift's variant is broader than objc's because Swift's type\ninference is pervasive, so `let x = foo()` leaves no written type at all --\nwhich is why 16.5% is a THIRD of objc's 50.2% and a quarter of java's 65.0%.\n\nEXPOSURE: 93 of swift's 107 catalogue rows are method-kind and 0 are R2-only,\nso the receiver-typing route is effectively swift's ENTIRE catalogue. There is\nno second disjunct to fall back on the way go has package qualifiers, erlang has\ncall-site modules, and C now has `#include` (WI-lajus).\n\nDIRECTION WARNING, per INV-linub's own rule: more typed receivers feed more\nresolved callees, which feeds section 7a sanitizer registration, and a\nregistered barrier earns `sanitized` and DROPS the flow (#214). Measure at L4\non findings, in both directions. WI-lajus is the live cautionary case from the\nsame day -- its typed-receiver win moved 15 of 21 claim verdicts toward\nwithholding.\n\nONE REPOSITORY. vapor is 4 MB and the smallest subject in the study; the 16.5%\nis a single-repo number and is not claimed to generalise."  # 73cd
